      "ROSE: No, a year of partying is enough. She'll be going to Harvard this fall.\nELIZABETH: I haven't been accepted yet, mother.\nROSE: If you think Michael Dukakis will provide for this country prior to the point when you decide to squeeze one out, then I think you're misinf…\nSAMANTHA: When can I squeeze one out?",
      "ROSE: When did you stop taking your medication?\nELIZABETH: Did you just call me a fuck-ass?\nROSE: That's enough.\nELIZABETH: You can suck a fuck.",
      "ROSE: We will not have this kind of language at the dinner table.\nSAMANTHA: What's a fuck-ass?",
      "SAMANTHA: If it fell from a plane, then what happened to the plane?\nELIZABETH: They don't know, Samantha.\nSAMANTHA: Is there any way that we can make money from this? Couldn't we get on television if we sue the airline?",
      "SAMANTHA: I'm telling Mom.\nELIZABETH: Samantha, don't go over there."
    ]
